---
import '../styles/tokens/skyfield.generated.css';
import sceneRaw from '../assets/skyfield-scene.svg?raw';

/* The landscape: the stage-4 traced scene. A 2028x1108 geometry traced from
   public/images/reference_bg.png — snow-capped summit with crevasses, ridge bands,
   the river and terraces, green hills, the foreground forest with the wizard painted
   into it, sun with its measured radial glow. Everything is generated: gen_stage4.py
   (parity/stage4/) emits the SVG and its 313-token relighting CSS from the traced
   dawn scene plus the Day/Dusk/Night variant images; emit_site.py adapts both for
   the site. Do not edit the scene or its CSS here.

   Time of day rides the same html[data-time] attribute Base.astro stamps pre-paint
   (dawn is the base state). The tokens tween over --t-sky, the sun physically
   travels to its per-state seat, and overlay groups (stars, moon, dusk rim, birds
   at day only) fade per state. prefers-reduced-motion snaps all of it, via both the
   generated transition:none block and motion.css zeroing --dur-sky.

   Purely presentational — time stamping lives in Base.astro, the preview control in
   the page that wants one. */
---

<div class="skyfield" aria-hidden="true" set:html={sceneRaw} />

<style>
  .skyfield {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .skyfield :global(svg) {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
  }
</style>
